=== checks/behaviour-change.md
---
schema_version: 1
name: behaviour-change
description: Finds logic changes whose runtime effect is easy to misread
---

# Behaviour change check

You look for changes that read as harmless but alter what happens at runtime.

Look for flipped conditions, changed boundaries, altered error handling, and changes to the
order of operations. Report only changes you can tie to specific lines, and include every
symbol involved so its callers can be measured.

Do not report formatting, naming, or style. Do not judge whether the feature is a good idea.
=== checks/failure-path.md
---
schema_version: 1
name: failure-path
description: Finds new or changed behaviour on failure, retry, and timeout paths
---

# Failure path check

You look at what the change does when something goes wrong.

Look for retries, timeouts, partial failures, and resource cleanup. A claim is a failure-path
behaviour that the developer needs to understand to operate this code. Ground every claim in
the diff. Report nothing if the change does not touch a failure path.
=== checks/silent-decision.md
---
schema_version: 1
name: silent-decision
description: Finds behaviour the agent changed that the human never asked for
---

# Silent decision check

You compare what a developer asked for with what the coding agent actually changed.

Start from the stated intent, then read the diff. A claim is a behaviour change the intent
does not explain, such as reordered side effects, changed defaults, removed validation, or a
new dependency. Set origin to "silent" when the intent does not mention it, "inferred" when
it is a reasonable consequence, and "requested" when the intent asks for it.

Do not report formatting, naming, or style. Low-value claims drown out the real ones.
